# Budapest

Budapest, the capital of Hungary, is known for its scenic setting along the Danube River, stunning architecture, and rich history.

## Buda Castle

Buda Castle is a historical castle and palace complex of the Hungarian kings in Budapest. It now houses the Hungarian National Gallery and The Budapest History Museum.
> TIP: Visit in the evening to see the castle beautifully lit up.
![open1](./buda_castle.jpeg)
![openFra](./buda_castle2.jpeg)

## Parliament Building

The Hungarian Parliament Building is one of the most iconic landmarks in Budapest. It is the largest building in Hungary and a stunning example of Gothic Revival architecture.
> Don't miss the guided tours to explore the interior.
![open1](./parliament.jpeg)
![openFra](./parliament2.jpeg)

## Széchenyi Thermal Bath

The Széchenyi Thermal Bath is one of the largest spa complexes in Europe. It offers a range of indoor and outdoor pools, saunas, and wellness treatments.
> TIP: Visit early in the morning or late in the evening to avoid the crowds.
![open1](./thermal_bath.jpeg)
![openFra](./thermal_bath2.jpeg)

## Budapest Cuisine

> TIP: Must-try dishes include goulash, lángos, chimney cake, and a variety of Hungarian pastries. Don't forget to sample the local wines and pálinka.
